   "subject": "geom_ribbon cutting off weirdly when intercepting with x-axis",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello! I just wanted to make a basic plot using geom_ribbon. Here&#39;s an example:<div><br></div><div>Firstly I get my dataset:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">x_vec </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>y_vec </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> seq</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">200</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></font><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x_vec</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y_vec</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#y=2x</span></div></code></div><br>This is essentially data of the form y=2x.</div><div><br></div><div>Then I plot it using geom_ribbon as such:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>      geom_ribbon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ymax</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ymin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></font><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">#make a semi-transparent ribbon</span><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      scale_y_continuous</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">limits</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\">expand</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#set the limits </span><span style=\"color:#800\">and remove and margins within the plot for </span></font><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(136,0,0)\">y-</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(136,0,0)\">axis </span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"> </span></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">      scale_x_continuous</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">expand</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#remove margins within plot for x-axis</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br></div><div>And I obtain this:</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-QgLehjOunOg/VX5qCQ5ZReI/AAAAAAAAAjA/0bRLWAuBSe8/s1600/Rplot01.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-QgLehjOunOg/VX5qCQ5ZReI/AAAAAAAAAjA/0bRLWAuBSe8/s1600/Rplot01.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369001170000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Yt4bUluMo1VMm9X3sxlZq\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-QgLehjOunOg/VX5qCQ5ZReI/AAAAAAAAAjA/0bRLWAuBSe8/s320/Rplot01.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"295\" height=\"320\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">As you can see, the ribbon does this ugly thing where it cuts of vertically instead of going all the way to the x-axis. I would like to get something like this (which I did quickly using paint just for demonstration):<br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-y-U0noss4UY/VX5rPQWtbZI/AAAAAAAAAjQ/R6XoOLD8z18/s1600/Rplot02.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-y-U0noss4UY/VX5rPQWtbZI/AAAAAAAAAjQ/R6XoOLD8z18/s1600/Rplot02.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369001170000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3h4dMKQHIhvhT494gtlI2x\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-y-U0noss4UY/VX5rPQWtbZI/AAAAAAAAAjQ/R6XoOLD8z18/s320/Rplot02.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"295\" height=\"320\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">Can anyone help me with that? Thank you :)</p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "1Z45sk446QQJ",
   "from": "Richard Zijdeman",
   "author": "463b8c05680be401",
   "date": "2015-06-15T11:10:37Z",
   "subject": "Re: geom_ribbon cutting off weirdly when intercepting with x-axis",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hi, thanks for you well setup question. Since you refer to the behaviour as ‘ugly’ I was wondering whether your point is just about aesthetics and if so, if you’re really ready to modify appropriate plotting behaviour. Ribbon adds colour directly above and below the plotted point, not to the side of a plotted point. What you’re asking for is different plotting behaviour at the extremes of your x-variable. Add ‘+ geom_point’ to your plot, and you’ll see that everywhere the grey ribbon is appropriately plotted.<div><br></div><div>Good luck,</div><div><br></div><div>Richard</div><div><br><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div><br></div><div><br><div><br></div><div><br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On 15 Jun 2015, at 08:08, rajivkk1 &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">raji...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello! I just wanted to make a basic plot using geom_ribbon. Here&#39;s an example:<div><br></div><div>Firstly I get my dataset:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><font color=\"#660066\"><span>x_vec </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span><br>y_vec </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> seq</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">200</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br></span></font>data <span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span> data<span style=\"color:#660\">.</span>frame<span style=\"color:#660\">(</span>x<span style=\"color:#660\">=</span>x_vec<span style=\"color:#660\">,</span>y<span style=\"color:#660\">=</span>y_vec<span style=\"color:#660\">)</span> <span style=\"color:#800\">#y=2x</span></code></div><br>This is essentially data of the form y=2x.</div><div><br></div><div>Then I plot it using geom_ribbon as such:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span>ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span>y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span> <br>      geom_ribbon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>ymax</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span>ymin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span> alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span> </span></font><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">#make a semi-transparent ribbon</span><font color=\"#660066\"><span><br>      scale_y_continuous</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>limits</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span>expand</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#set the limits </span><span style=\"color:#800\">and remove and margins within the plot for </span></font><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(136,0,0)\">y-</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(136,0,0)\">axis </span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"> </span></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span>      scale_x_continuous</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>expand</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#remove margins within plot for x-axis</span></font><span><br></span></div></code></div><br></div><div>And I obtain this:</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-QgLehjOunOg/VX5qCQ5ZReI/AAAAAAAAAjA/0bRLWAuBSe8/s1600/Rplot01.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-QgLehjOunOg/VX5qCQ5ZReI/AAAAAAAAAjA/0bRLWAuBSe8/s1600/Rplot01.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369001176000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ASaeUQJjJyBHFbcz6U5w1\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-QgLehjOunOg/VX5qCQ5ZReI/AAAAAAAAAjA/0bRLWAuBSe8/s320/Rplot01.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"295\" height=\"320\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">As you can see, the ribbon does this ugly thing where it cuts of vertically instead of going all the way to the x-axis. I would like to get something like this (which I did quickly using paint just for demonstration):<br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-y-U0noss4UY/VX5rPQWtbZI/AAAAAAAAAjQ/R6XoOLD8z18/s1600/Rplot02.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-y-U0noss4UY/VX5rPQWtbZI/AAAAAAAAAjQ/R6XoOLD8z18/s1600/Rplot02.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369001176000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1LUGrZKOtkigoBZUsyKHEP\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-y-U0noss4UY/VX5rPQWtbZI/AAAAAAAAAjQ/R6XoOLD8z18/s320/Rplot02.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"295\" height=\"320\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">Can anyone help me with that? Thank you :)</p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><div><br></div></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
